[1mHarness design decisions worth knowing[22m, since they were forced by the C's behaviour rather than chosen:[0m[0m
[0m[0m
- Every call runs in a forked child, so a failed [38;5;10massert()[0m (SIGABRT) or SIGSEGV becomes a comparable outcome. The two children are forked back-to-back from identical parent state, so glibc's arena matches and even the C's reads of uninitialised heap are reproducible.[0m[0m
- The child's stderr is captured to a memfd, which is how I can prove [3mwhich[23m assertion a given input reaches rather than just "it aborted" — e.g. row A1 needed a 386-case targeted search, and 3 cases are confirmed to hit [38;5;10mlib.c:80: cp_ptr[0m.[0m[0m
- Children are marked [38;5;10mPR_SET_DUMPABLE=0[0m; this host pipes cores to systemd-coredump, which cost ~0.6 s per SIGABRT across thousands of aborting cases.[0m[0m
